      ./../../tests/rhai_scan_file.rs, ./../../tests/rhai_scan_gitlab.rs,
      ./../../tests/rhai_scan_http.rs — today 14 test fns touch this script (10 run it, 4
      run copied snippets), and the four snippet tests must be rewritten to run the file.
  [ ] Add the unmapped coverage: the waypoint-chain Scenario (too-new skip, min-previous
      skip, both stop-legs, un-annotated stop), cluster record-then-rethrow, file-lane
      `SCAN-FILE-001` masking, the anonymous-credential probe, and the s3 lane (no s3
      registration exists on any test engine today).
  [?] Credential binding mismatch — VERDICT frozen here: ./scan.rhai reads the four
      credential keys exclusively from `args.keys()` and defines no bare-global reads, while
      /agent/src/boxes/scan.sdd binds them as scope globals the file never references and
      serializes an `args` that can never carry those keys — the fetched credentials are dead
      on arrival and both lanes scan cache sources anonymously. Decide the fix side (Rust
      merges into `args` vs the script reads the bare globals) and whether present-as-null
      keys get an `!= ()` leg so they degrade to anonymous instead of crashing.
  [?] Confirm the chain-stop legs are intended: a first un-annotated tag aborts enumeration
      of all older tags (a mirror/republished catalog with one foreign tag at the top hides
      the whole chain), and the first base version accepted without a minimum also stops the
      walk — decide whether a skip-and-continue leg belongs here.
  [?] The too-new @print diagnostic interpolates the already-advanced `iter_tags` next to
      `current` and carries the `requiere` typo; it goes to stdout where every other scan
      message goes to @log_info/@log_warn — decide the message, channel and text.
  [?] @union_packages dedups by `tag` alone — safe only because each call spans one image;
      decide whether to key on `registry`+`image`+`tag` before any reuse beyond the
      per-image triple-maturity union.
  [?] The `script` source lane gets a fresh-scope @eval (no `box`/`args`/`spec`, no helpers
      from this file) — confirm the snippet-is-self-contained contract and how an evaluated
      snippet is meant to enumerate registries at all.
  [?] @json_encode(e) of a structural (non-string) engine error inside the catch may fail on
      the boxed payload, escaping with no failed-status recorded — verify the engine behavior
      live and decide a safe serialization posture.

Done when:
  Every Scenario has a mapped passing test (or a carried Task exemption), the
    credential-binding decision is implemented on one side and mirrored here, the chain-stop
    and diagnostic decisions are recorded, and the test/clippy/fmt/specdd harness stays green.
